      "id": 1,
      "text": "After the 1923 Great Kanto Earthquake, Asagaya grew into a literary enclave when the JR Asagaya station opened in 1922.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://experience-suginami.tokyo/asagaya/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Asagaya earned the nickname “Literary Town Asagaya” because of its historic writers’ gatherings.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Asagaya"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Asagaya Shinmeigu Shrine, a historic Shinto site, features a dragon‑carved stone gate that locals admire.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://japanmapper.com/area-guide/asagaya"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Asagaya Jazz Street festival draws musicians to multiple venues, making it one of Tokyo’s largest jazz events.",
